    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618-a1">

                <pb facs="0792" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg698"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 115.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eckford to Mr. Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Kingston, Jamaica</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 181.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>. Referring to my dispatch No. 180, dated the
                    28th day of March, I have the honor to inclose the affidavit of the master and
                    mate of the American schooner <hi rendition="#italic">William Todd</hi>, in
                    reference to the firing upon and search of the said vessel by two Spanish
                    gunboats.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Q. O. Eckford.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
